.\" Manual page for sessium.
.\" View with:  man docs/sessium.1
.TH SESSIUM 1 "2026-11-04" "sessium 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sessium \- git-like version control for Claude Code sessions, with Google Drive as the remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sessium
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sessium
backs up Claude Code conversations to Google Drive (via
.BR rclone (1))
and restores them on any machine. Your
.I ~/.claude/projects
tree is the "repo", Drive is the "remote", and a per-machine ledger
(~/.local/state/sessium/state.json) records what was last synced — the
".git" of the arrangement.
.PP
A session id is the transcript file's UUID stem. A prefix of it is accepted
wherever an
.I id
argument appears. A project's
.I munged
name is its absolute path with every "/" replaced by "\-" (leading slash
included), e.g. \fI/home/me/repo\fR → \fI\-home\-me\-repo\fR. Windows munges
every separator and the drive colon the same way.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR list " [\-\-titles] [\-\-project " \fImunged\fR "]"
List every session found locally or on Drive, newest first. With
.B \-\-titles
shows each session's first real user message. Alias:
.BR log .
.TP
.BR status " [\-\-project " \fImunged\fR "]"
Classify every session against the ledger and Drive: in-sync, push, pull,
CONFLICT, new-here, new-there. Read-only; never touches anything.
.TP
.B check
Six-step self-test: rclone present, remote reachable, folder exists, local
claude dir, ledger, session counts.
.TP
.BR setup " [\-\-check\-only]"
Run setup\-ubuntu.sh (interactive rclone install + Drive OAuth).
.TP
.BR push " [\-\-project " \fImunged\fR "]"
Upload new and locally-changed sessions. Conflicts are
.B skipped
with a warning — sync or resolve decides them. Never deletes from Drive.
.TP
.BR pull " [\-\-project " \fImunged\fR "]"
Download new and remotely-changed sessions. Skips conflicts like push.
.TP
.BR sync " [\-\-interactive] [\-\-project " \fImunged\fR "]"
Push and pull what changed in one pass, and
.B decide conflicts:
on a terminal it prompts
.BR [L]ocal / [R]emote / [B]oth " "(newest " wins ") / [S]kip ;
without one (cron, pipes) the newest copy wins automatically. The losing
copy is never deleted — it becomes a revert file.
.TP
.BR diff " <id> [\-\-project " \fImunged\fR "]"
Show one session side by side: local vs remote size, mtime, message count,
last snippet, and the ledger's record.
.TP
.BR resolve " <id> [\-\-interactive]"
Manually decide a conflicted session (same prompt as sync). Non-conflicted
sessions are a no-op.
.TP
.B revert " <id>"
List the session's revert copies (kept when conflicts were resolved) and
swap the chosen one back in; the copy it replaces is itself kept. Afterwards
.B sessium sync
pushes the restored copy.
.TP
.BR adopt " <munged-folder> <repo-path>"
Rehome sessions pulled for a different machine path so
.B claude \-\-resume
finds them here: copies transcripts and data folders (never the machine-local
revert/) under this machine's munged name. Identical files are skipped,
differing ones are kept
.B both
(yours untouched).
.TP
.B open " <id>"
Resume helper: resolve the session's project path and print the
.B cd + claude \-\-resume
command line to bring that conversation back up here.
.TP
.BR search " <query> [\-\-project " \fImunged\fR "] [\-\-limit N] [\-\-semantic]"
Search sessions: title matches outrank body matches. With
.B \-\-semantic
(and seeker configured) queries a self-hosted seeker engine for semantic
matching instead of literal text.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-project " " \fImunged\fR
Restrict a command to one project. Munged names start with "\-", which is
handled correctly in both space and equals forms.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output (list, status, diff, search). Schema in SPEC.md §9.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print exactly what the command would do — push, pull, sync, revert, adopt —
and change nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-interactive
Force the conflict prompt even when no terminal is attached.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print every rclone invocation.
.TP
.B \-\-titles
(list) Show session titles.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SESSIUM_CLAUDE_DIR
Claude data root (default ~/.claude).
.TP
.B SESSIUM_CONFIG
Config file path (default ~/.config/sessium/config.json).
.TP
.B SESSIUM_STATE
Ledger path (default ~/.local/state/sessium/state.json).
.TP
.B SESSIUM_RCLONE_BIN
rclone binary (default "rclone" on PATH).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sessium/config.json
{"rclone_remote": "...", "drive_folder": "..."}; legacy ~/sessium/config.sh
(DRIVE_REMOTE / DRIVE_DIR) still read as a fallback.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sessium/state.json
The ledger — per-machine, never synced.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/<munged>/revert/
Machine-local revert copies; never synced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success — skips are not failures. 1 on real failures. 130 when
interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
rclone(1), claude(1). Project docs: README.md, SPEC.md, PLAN.md,
docs/BUILD.md in the repository.
